<section class="memory-example example-personal" id="how-it-works" aria-labelledby="personal-example-title">
  <div class="example-layout">
    <div class="example-heading">
      <h2 id="personal-example-title">Find the <br />detail again.</h2>
      <p>A quick note is enough. Add a detail when you need to, then find what you meant with the original still there.</p>
      <a class="memo-button memo-button-primary" href="https://app.memoato.com" rel="noreferrer" referrerpolicy="no-referrer">Try personal memory<svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 10h11M11 6l4 4-4 4"></path></svg></a>
    </div>

    <figure class="memory-example-flow" aria-labelledby="personal-example-caption">
      <figcaption id="personal-example-caption">Personal memory · Fictional example</figcaption>
      <ol class="example-steps" role="list">
        <li id="personal-example-note">
          <h3>Capture</h3>
          <div>
            <blockquote>Lunch at Maru with Sam. Order the miso aubergine again.</blockquote>
            <p class="example-meta">Your original note · 12 May</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Review</h3>
          <div>
            <dl class="remembered-details">
              <div><dt>Remember</dt><dd>Order the miso aubergine again.</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Place</dt><dd><del>Maru</del> <ins>Maru on Market Street</ins></dd></div>
            </dl>
            <p class="example-meta">Place clarified by you. The original note stays unchanged.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Recall</h3>
          <div>
            <p class="example-question">“What did I want to order again at Maru?”</p>
            <p class="example-answer">The miso aubergine.</p>
            <a class="example-source-link" href="#personal-example-note">View the original lunch note</a>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="memory-example example-project" id="ai-context" aria-labelledby="context-title">
  <div class="example-layout">
    <div class="example-heading">
      <h2 id="context-title">Context you <br />can check.</h2>
      <p>Bring a project source, review the claim, and give AI an answer that points back to the evidence.</p>
      <p class="example-availability">Context is in pilot: one owner per workspace, with read-only GitHub and Linear sources.</p>
      <div class="example-actions">
        <a class="memo-button memo-button-light" href="mailto:hello@memoato.com?subject=Memoato%20Context%20pilot">Ask about the pilot<svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 10h11M11 6l4 4-4 4"></path></svg></a>
        <a class="example-source-link" href="https://guide.hills-lab.hr" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read the approach</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <figure class="memory-example-flow" aria-labelledby="project-example-caption">
      <figcaption id="project-example-caption">Project context · Fictional example</figcaption>
      <ol class="example-steps" role="list">
        <li id="project-example-source">
          <h3>Source</h3>
          <div>
            <blockquote>Retry transient sync failures in the worker. The API accepts the job and returns.</blockquote>
            <p class="example-meta">GitHub · docs/sync-retries.md · Version 2</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Review</h3>
          <div>
            <p class="reviewed-claim">Retries run in the background worker.</p>
            <p class="example-meta">Accepted by the workspace owner.</p>
            <dl class="source-checks">
              <div><dt>Freshness</dt><dd>Within its review window</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Access</dt><dd>Within the allowed project scope</dd></div>
            </dl>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Retrieve</h3>
          <div>
            <p class="example-question">“Where should sync retries run?”</p>
            <p class="example-answer">In the worker, so the API can return without waiting.</p>
            <a class="example-source-link" href="#project-example-source">View the GitHub source example</a>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

